   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Am I Born to Die** (1 review): The reviewer says the soundboard version of this song alone justifies downloading the recording [2]\n- **A Letter to Seymour** (1 review): The song is by Dave Bruzza of Greensky Bluegrass, and the reviewer notes a shoutout to Bruzza [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **White Freightliner Blues**: rare: 13 archived performances [4]\n- **A Letter to Seymour**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 9 archived performances [4]\n- **Ten Degrees and Getting Colder**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [4]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Living Like an Animal, Am I Born to Die [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2017-11-09.sbd.flac16** (recommended): soundboard; 14 songs; 80 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: The reviewer describes the recording as a soundboard source [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2017-11-09.sbd.flac16**: taped by Ken Tredway; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: soundboard>SD722 [1]. Also: Transfer chain: SD722 recorder, edited in Sound Forge Pro 11 with fades and iZotope 64-bit SRC, then MBIT+ conversion to 16-bit/44.1kHz; After editing, the files were tracked in CDWAV and encoded to FLAC with Trader's Little Helper [1]",
